                    <birth when="1788-12-16">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1849-01-20"/>
                    <occupation>bookseller</occupation>
                    <occupation>publisher</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Cadell became a clerk and eventually, in 1811, a partner in <persName key="CON01">Archibald Constable's</persName> publishing house. He was a personal 
      professional friend of <persName key="SCO03">Sir Walter Scott</persName> and 
      was closely involved in many of his publications, notably the author's edition of <title>Waverley</title> in 1827.  </p>
                        <p>Godwin met Cadell in 1816 on his trip to Scotland and subsequently wrote to him in 1830 with a view to selling him the copyright to a new work, probably 
      <title corresp="thou01">Thoughts on Man</title>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS">MS. Abinger c. 20, fol. 25r; 7 July 1830</bibl>
